            "children": [
              {
                "id": "cn5zrt4t4zbdp6z",
                "text": "Free Energy: Summary"
              }
            ],
            "id": "467yso061z0lgpw",
            "type": "h1"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Gibbs free energy ("
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "G"
              },
              {
                "text": ") is a state function defined with regard to system quantities only and may be used to predict the spontaneity of a process. A negative value for ΔG indicates a spontaneous process; a positive ΔG indicates a nonspontaneous process; and a ΔG of zero indicates that the system is at equilibrium. A number of approaches to the computation of free energy changes are possible."
              }
            ],
            "id": "vym0ndge3k1wkph",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "0czfkphh9radno6",
                "text": "End of Lesson Self-Assessment"
              }
            ],
            "id": "wse6vi33vsf00e6",
            "type": "h1"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Before you take the checkpoint, please evaluate your understanding of the learning objectives for the module "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "Free Energy"
              },
              {
                "text": " and use the My Response link below to ask any questions you might have about the material that you would like the instructor to address. Your questions can be for clarification of the material or further insight. Your self-evaluation and questions may also shape the discussions in class."
              }
            ],
            "id": "wliq3kl93n5z3vj",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Your responses will not be graded, but will be available for your instructor."
              }
            ],
            "id": "slhsbnng2wseg80",
            "type": "p"
          },
